{"id": "ch41", "number": "41", "title": "Proofs and semantics", "titleInlines": [{"type": "text", "text": "Proofs and semantics"}], "part": "VII", "blocks": [{"type": "para", "children": [{"type": "text", "text": "We have used two different turnstiles in this book. This:"}]}, {"type": "displaymath", "latex": "\\mathcal{A}_1, \\mathcal{A}_2, \\ldots, \\mathcal{A}_n \\vdash \\mathcal{C}"}, {"type": "para", "children": [{"type": "text", "text": "means that there is some proof which ends with "}, {"type": "math", "latex": "\\mathcal{C}", "display": false}, {"type": "text", "text": " and whose only undischarged assumptions are among "}, {"type": "math", "latex": "\\mathcal{A}_1, \\mathcal{A}_2, \\ldots, \\mathcal{A}_n", "display": false}, {"type": "text", "text": ". This is a "}, {"type": "emph", "children": [{"type": "text", "text": "proof-theoretic notion"}]}, {"type": "text", "text": ". By contrast, this:"}]}, {"type": "displaymath", "latex": "\\mathcal{A}_1, \\mathcal{A}_2, \\ldots, \\mathcal{A}_n \\vDash \\mathcal{C}"}, {"type": "para", "children": [{"type": "text", "text": "means that no valuation (or interpretation) makes all of "}, {"type": "math", "latex": "\\mathcal{A}_1, \\mathcal{A}_2, \\ldots, \\mathcal{A}_n", "display": false}, {"type": "text", "text": " true and "}, {"type": "math", "latex": "\\mathcal{C}", "display": false}, {"type": "text", "text": " false. This concerns assignments of truth and falsity to sentences. It is a "}, {"type": "emph", "children": [{"type": "text", "text": "semantic notion"}]}, {"type": "text", "text": "."}]}, {"type": "para", "children": [{"type": "text", "text": "It cannot be emphasized enough that these are different notions. But we can emphasize it a bit more: "}, {"type": "emph", "children": [{"type": "text", "text": "They are different notions."}]}]}, {"type": "para", "children": [{"type": "text", "text": "Once you have internalised this point, continue reading."}]}, {"type": "para", "children": [{"type": "text", "text": "Although our semantic and proof-theoretic notions are different, there is a deep connection between them. To explain this connection,we will start by considering the relationship between validities and theorems."}]}, {"type": "para", "children": [{"type": "text", "text": "To show that a sentence is a theorem, you need only produce a proof. Granted, it may be hard to produce a twenty line proof, but it is not so hard to check each line of the proof and confirm that it is legitimate; and if each line of the proof individually is legitimate, then the whole proof is legitimate. Showing that a sentence is a validity, though, requires reasoning about all possible interpretations. Given a choice between showing that a sentence is a theorem and showing that it is a validity, it would be easier to show that it is a theorem."}]}, {"type": "para", "children": [{"type": "text", "text": "Contrawise, to show that a sentence is "}, {"type": "emph", "children": [{"type": "text", "text": "not"}]}, {"type": "text", "text": " a theorem is hard. We would need to reason about all (possible) proofs. That is very difficult. However, to show that a sentence is not a validity, you need only construct an interpretation in which the sentence is false. Granted, it may be hard to come up with the interpretation; but once you have done so, it is relatively straightforward to check what truth value it assigns to a sentence. Given a choice between showing that a sentence is not a theorem and showing that it is not a validity, it would be easier to show that it is not a validity."}]}, {"type": "para", "children": [{"type": "text", "text": "Fortunately, "}, {"type": "emph", "children": [{"type": "text", "text": "a sentence is a theorem if and only if it is a validity"}]}, {"type": "text", "text": ". As a result, if we provide a proof of "}, {"type": "math", "latex": "\\mathcal{A}", "display": false}, {"type": "text", "text": " on no assumptions, and thus show that "}, {"type": "math", "latex": "\\mathcal{A}", "display": false}, {"type": "text", "text": " is a theorem, i.e., "}, {"type": "math", "latex": "{}\\vdash \\mathcal{A}", "display": false}, {"type": "text", "text": ", we can legitimately infer that "}, {"type": "math", "latex": "\\mathcal{A}", "display": false}, {"type": "text", "text": " is a validity, i.e., "}, {"type": "math", "latex": "\\vDash \\mathcal{A}", "display": false}, {"type": "text", "text": ". Similarly, if we construct an interpretation in which "}, {"type": "math", "latex": "\\mathcal{A}"}, {"type": "text", "text": " is false and thus show that it is not a validity, i.e., "}, {"type": "math", "latex": "\\nvDash \\mathcal{A}", "display": false}, {"type": "text", "text": ", it follows that "}, {"type": "math", "latex": "\\mathcal{A}"}, {"type": "text", "text": " is not a theorem, i.e., "}, {"type": "math", "latex": "\\nvdash \\mathcal{A}", "display": false}, {"type": "text", "text": "."}]}, {"type": "para", "children": [{"type": "text", "text": "More generally, we have the following powerful result:"}]}, {"type": "factoid", "children": [{"type": "para", "children": [{"type": "math", "latex": "\\mathcal{A}_1, \\mathcal{A}_2, \\ldots, \\mathcal{A}_n \\vdash \\mathcal{B}", "display": false}, {"type": "text", "text": " "}, {"type": "strong", "children": [{"type": "text", "text": "iff"}]}, {"type": "text", "text": " "}, {"type": "math", "latex": "\\mathcal{A}_1, \\mathcal{A}_2, \\ldots, \\mathcal{A}_n \\vDash \\mathcal{B}", "display": false}]}]}, {"type": "para", "children": [{"type": "text", "text": "This shows that, whilst provability and entailment are "}, {"type": "emph", "children": [{"type": "text", "text": "different"}]}, {"type": "text", "text": " notions, they are extensionally equivalent. As such:"}]}, {"type": "factoid", "children": [{"type": "list", "kind": "factoiditems", "items": [{"children": [{"type": "para", "children": [{"type": "text", "text": "An argument is "}, {"type": "emph", "children": [{"type": "text", "text": "valid"}]}, {"type": "text", "text": " iff "}, {"type": "emph", "children": [{"type": "text", "text": "the conclusion can be proved from the premises"}]}, {"type": "text", "text": "."}]}]}, {"children": [{"type": "para", "children": [{"type": "text", "text": "A sentence is a "}, {"type": "emph", "children": [{"type": "text", "text": "validity"}]}, {"type": "text", "text": " iff it is a "}, {"type": "emph", "children": [{"type": "text", "text": "theorem"}]}, {"type": "text", "text": "."}]}]}, {"children": [{"type": "para", "children": [{"type": "text", "text": "Two sentences are "}, {"type": "emph", "children": [{"type": "text", "text": "equivalent"}]}, {"type": "text", "text": " iff they are "}, {"type": "emph", "children": [{"type": "text", "text": "interderivable"}]}, {"type": "text", "text": "."}]}]}, {"children": [{"type": "para", "children": [{"type": "text", "text": "Sentences are "}, {"type": "emph", "children": [{"type": "text", "text": "jointly satisfiable"}]}, {"type": "text", "text": " iff they are "}, {"type": "emph", "children": [{"type": "text", "text": "jointly consistent"}]}, {"type": "text", "text": "."}]}]}]}]}, {"type": "para", "children": [{"type": "text", "text": "For this reason, you can pick and choose when to think in terms of proofs and when to think in terms of valuations/interpretations, doing whichever is easier for a given task. The table on the next page summarizes which is (usually) easier."}]}, {"type": "para", "children": [{"type": "text", "text": "It is intuitive that provability and semantic entailment should agree. But—let us repeat this—do not be fooled by the similarity of the symbols ‘"}, {"type": "math", "latex": "\\vDash", "display": false}, {"type": "text", "text": "’ and ‘"}, {"type": "math", "latex": "\\vdash", "display": false}, {"type": "text", "text": "’. These two symbols have very different meanings. The fact that provability and semantic entailment agree is not an easy result to come by."}]}, {"type": "para", "children": [{"type": "text", "text": "In fact, demonstrating that provability and semantic entailment agree is, very decisively, the point at which introductory logic becomes intermediate logic."}]}, {"type": "center", "children": [{"type": "table", "cols": [{"kind": "l", "align": "left", "borderLeft": 0}, {"kind": "l", "align": "left", "borderLeft": 0}, {"kind": "l", "align": "left", "borderLeft": 0}], "rows": [{"cells": [{"children": []}, {"children": [{"type": "strong", "children": [{"type": "text", "text": "Yes"}]}]}, {"children": [{"type": "strong", "children": [{"type": "text", "text": "No"}]}]}], "hlineBefore": 0}, {"cells": [{"children": [{"type": "text", "text": "[12pt] Is "}, {"type": "math", "latex": "\\mathcal{A}"}, {"type": "text", "text": " a "}, {"type": "strong", "children": [{"type": "text", "text": "validity"}]}, {"type": "text", "text": "?"}]}, {"children": [{"type": "text", "text": "give a proof which shows "}, {"type": "math", "latex": "\\vdash \\mathcal{A}", "display": false}]}, {"children": [{"type": "text", "text": "give an interpretation in which "}, {"type": "math", "latex": "\\mathcal{A}"}, {"type": "text", "text": " is false"}]}], "hlineBefore": 0}, {"cells": [{"children": [{"type": "text", "text": "[12pt] Is "}, {"type": "math", "latex": "\\mathcal{A}"}, {"type": "text", "text": " a "}, {"type": "strong", "children": [{"type": "text", "text": "contradiction"}]}, {"type": "text", "text": "?"}]}, {"children": [{"type": "text", "text": "give a proof which shows "}, {"type": "math", "latex": "\\mathcal{A} \\vdash \\bot", "display": false}]}, {"children": [{"type": "text", "text": "give an interpretation in which "}, {"type": "math", "latex": "\\mathcal{A}"}, {"type": "text", "text": " is true"}]}], "hlineBefore": 0}, {"cells": [{"children": [{"type": "text", "text": "[12pt] Are "}, {"type": "math", "latex": "\\mathcal{A}"}, {"type": "text", "text": " and "}, {"type": "math", "latex": "\\mathcal{B}"}, {"type": "text", "text": " "}, {"type": "strong", "children": [{"type": "text", "text": "equivalent"}]}, {"type": "text", "text": "?"}]}, {"children": [{"type": "text", "text": "give two proofs, one for "}, {"type": "math", "latex": "\\mathcal{A}\\vdash \\mathcal{B}", "display": false}, {"type": "text", "text": " and one for "}, {"type": "math", "latex": "\\mathcal{B}\\vdash \\mathcal{A}", "display": false}]}, {"children": [{"type": "text", "text": "give an interpretation in which "}, {"type": "math", "latex": "\\mathcal{A}"}, {"type": "text", "text": " and "}, {"type": "math", "latex": "\\mathcal{B}"}, {"type": "text", "text": " have different truth values"}]}], "hlineBefore": 0}, {"cells": [{"children": [{"type": "text", "text": "[12pt] Are "}, {"type": "math", "latex": "\\mathcal{A}_1, \\mathcal{A}_2, \\ldots, \\mathcal{A}_n", "display": false}, {"type": "text", "text": " "}, {"type": "strong", "children": [{"type": "text", "text": "jointly satisfiable"}]}, {"type": "text", "text": "?"}]}, {"children": [{"type": "text", "text": "give an interpretation in which all of "}, {"type": "math", "latex": "\\mathcal{A}_1, \\mathcal{A}_2, \\ldots, \\mathcal{A}_n", "display": false}, {"type": "text", "text": " are true"}]}, {"children": [{"type": "text", "text": "prove a contradiction from assumptions "}, {"type": "math", "latex": "\\mathcal{A}_1, \\mathcal{A}_2, \\ldots, \\mathcal{A}_n", "display": false}]}], "hlineBefore": 0}, {"cells": [{"children": [{"type": "text", "text": "[12pt] Is "}, {"type": "math", "latex": "\\mathcal{A}_1, \\mathcal{A}_2, \\ldots, \\mathcal{A}_n \\therefore \\mathcal{C}", "display": false}, {"type": "text", "text": " "}, {"type": "strong", "children": [{"type": "text", "text": "valid"}]}, {"type": "text", "text": "?"}]}, {"children": [{"type": "text", "text": "give a proof with assumptions "}, {"type": "math", "latex": "\\mathcal{A}_1, \\mathcal{A}_2, \\ldots, \\mathcal{A}_n", "display": false}, {"type": "text", "text": " and concluding with "}, {"type": "math", "latex": "\\mathcal{C}"}]}, {"children": [{"type": "text", "text": "give an interpretation in which each of "}, {"type": "math", "latex": "\\mathcal{A}_1, \\mathcal{A}_2, \\ldots, \\mathcal{A}_n", "display": false}, {"type": "text", "text": " is true and "}, {"type": "math", "latex": "\\mathcal{C}"}, {"type": "text", "text": " is false"}]}], "hlineBefore": 0}], "truthTable": false}]}], "exercises": [], "footnotes": []}